    "body": "## Summary\n\n- Keep the original Rayhan battle card visible, including its attack and selected counterargument, while the scripted vote remains owned by Events.\n- Persist a randomized 2:2 first-four vote order and reserve vote five for the player; preserve 3-4 second delays and reload progress.\n- Put the current player first in the Rayhan Event title, remove the irrelevant resolved warning, and announce the player as winner only for this scripted tutorial result.\n- Disable manual voting in the guided tutorial at both UI and action layers, unlocking normal votes from the canonical first-independent-battle completion flag.\n- Keep exact Web/docs mirrors and refresh cache-busting references for changed scripts.\n\n## Validation on `bd95233c78d84dc3cb3549f14d4e50b2c8710017`\n\n- PASS: Rayhan reveal runtime/scope regression, demo activation routing, demo isolation, winner-chat emission, answer validation, and Rayhan post-win sequence.\n- PASS: focused vote regression covers all six shuffled first-four 2:2 permutations, fifth player vote, final 3:2, and every vote timer at 3000-4000 ms.\n- PASS: JavaScript/Python syntax, `git diff --check`, and six byte-identical Web/docs mirror pairs.\n- Built-in Codex Browser completed the fresh-start wrong-answer tutorial path. During voting, Battles retained the Rayhan argument and selected answer; Events showed `Тестер против Райхан`; manual vote controls were disabled and no Battles vote appeared. Browser showed progress 3/5 at 2:1, then player victory at 3:2. The result card retained the selected answer and only `Закрыть`; winner chat used `Тестер` once. Reload preserved the result and totals (3 REP, 12 money, 1 win) without a repeated award.\n- Vote timing and 2:2-after-four are verified by the focused regression; the browser snapshots did not capture that intermediate frame or measure wall-clock intervals. Browser console inspection was not performed. The prior DOM fixture failure came from calling `claimResume()` after synthetic state setup; resume restores persisted state and replaces that fixture before its assertion. Codex did not run the Playwright/Chromium script.\n- GitHub workflows: `telemetry-receiver-checks` run 38424641385 SUCCESS; `ai-forensics-evidence` run 38424641315 SUCCESS.\n\nPR remains Draft pending ChatGPT final review. No Safari acceptance or merge is claimed.",
